-- The MODULE-NAME permutation of `record_receiver_ident_value_only_field_order/`.
-- Same two declarations, same values, the two module names swapped so the OTHER
-- layout sorts first.
--
-- 🚨 PERMUTE THE MODULE NAMES, NOT THE IMPORT CLAUSES.  The defect class this pair
-- stands over decided a projection's record by module-NAME sort order (`sortUniqS`
-- over the mangled owner keys), which is invariant under clause order — so a
-- permutation differential over import clauses finds nothing here and would pass
-- for the wrong reason.  `test/import_order_fixtures/` covers clause order for the
-- SPELLING question; this cell covers name order for the IDENTITY question.
--
-- The correct answer cannot depend on what the modules are called, so it is the
-- same hand-derived `11,22,44,33`.  If this cell and its sibling ever disagree,
-- the selector has gone back to reading sort order.
--
-- 🚨 LIKE ITS SIBLING, THIS CELL'S LAYOUT HALF RE-GRADES PR #1395, NOT #1319 UNIT
-- 3 — derived from the typed Core IR, where every stamp is MANGLED
-- (`… "a" "zzmod__Cfg"`) and unit 3's arm stamps the UNMANGLED head name, so it
-- cannot be the producer.  Unit 3 is what makes the program ACCEPTED at all
-- (stubbed back out, it is refused at exit 1, #1376).  See the sibling's header
-- for the full dump and derivation.
import zzmod.{mkA}
import aamod.{mkZ}

main : <IO> Unit
main =
  putStrLn
    (intToString mkA.a
      ++ ","
      ++ intToString mkA.b
      ++ ","
      ++ intToString mkZ.a
      ++ ","
      ++ intToString mkZ.b)
